  "notes": "{遺跡|いせき} refers to the physical remains of past civilizations or historical sites — ruins, archaeological sites, and ancient settlements. Composed of {遺|い} (leave behind) + {跡|せき} (trace/remains).\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {遺跡|いせき}を{発掘|はっくつ}する: to excavate ruins\n- {遺跡|いせき}を{調査|ちょうさ}する: to survey/investigate ruins\n- {古代|こだい}{遺跡|いせき}: ancient ruins\n- {世界|せかい}{遺産|いさん}の{遺跡|いせき}: World Heritage ruins\n\nFAMOUS EXAMPLES:\n- {三内丸山|さんないまるやま}{遺跡|いせき}: Sannai-Maruyama site (Jomon period)\n- {吉野ヶ里|よしのがり}{遺跡|いせき}: Yoshinogari ruins (Yayoi period)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {史跡|しせき}: officially designated historic site\n- {遺物|いぶつ}: artifact, relic\n- {発掘|はっくつ}: excavation\n- {考古学|こうこがく}: archaeology",
